description:
Job Summary :

Medpace is a Clinical Research Organization that is rapidly growing across the globally. Due to our continued growth, we are in search of qualified and focused individuals for a vital role in our Core Lab department. Our Clinical Application Support provides multi Tiers support for clinical research and core lab platforms across Medical Imaging, ECG, connected medical devices, mobile applications, and virtualized workstations.This position will deliver timely, high-quality customer service to globally located end users and investigator sites by troubleshooting technical and workflow issues, tracking incidents through resolution, and performing software installation and validation activities. In addition, you will act as a key liaison between end users, internal development teams, core infrastructure teams, and external vendors to coordinate escalations and ensure seamless operations across clinical trials.

Responsibilities :

* Provide technical support for clinical research and core lab platforms, including Medical Imaging, ECG, connected medical devices, mobile applications, and virtualized workstations;
* Deliver timely, high-quality customer service to internal users, central readers and investigator sites located globally;
* Troubleshoot and resolve technical and workflow issues, escalating to the appropriate teams when needed;
* Log, track, and document incidents and service requests through resolution using the ticketing system;
* Perform software installation, configuration, testing, and validation activities in accordance with company procedures;
* Act as a liaison between end users, internal development teams, core infrastructure teams, and external vendors while maintaining the interests of end users;
* Coordinate escalations and follow up with stakeholders to ensure seamless operations across clinical trials;
* Create and maintain support documentation, knowledge base articles, and user guides;
* Ensure support activities comply with applicable regulatory standards (GCP, 21 CFR Part 11, HIPAA/GDPR); and
* Perform other system-related tasks to meet company objectives.

Qualifications :

* Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Biomedical Engineering, Life Sciences, or a related field (or equivalent experience);
* 1–3 years of application or technical support experience, preferably in a CRO, pharmaceutical, or clinical research environment;
* Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities;
* Excellent communication skills and ability to work cross-functionally with staff, vendors, and external users from multiple countries;
* Good organizational skills, very detail oriented, and flexible;
* Must be able to work concurrently on several issues and projects, each with specific requirements;
* Competent in installation and troubleshooting of software;
* Demonstrated ability to learn new technologies/applications; and
* Knowledge of Microsoft® Windows operating systems.

**Preferred Qualifications**

* Hands-on familiarity with virtualized environments, mobile/device support, and ticketing systems; and
* Understanding of regulatory standards such as GCP, 21 CFR Part 11, and HIPAA/GDPR.

Medpace Overview :

Medpace is a full-service clinical contract research organization (CRO). We provide Phase I-IV clinical development services to the biotechnology, pharmaceutical and medical device industries. Our mission is to accelerate the global development of safe and effective medical therapeutics through its scientific and disciplined approach. We leverage local regulatory and therapeutic expertise across all major areas including oncology, cardiology, metabolic disease, endocrinology, central nervous system, anti-viral and anti-infective. Headquartered in Cincinnati, Ohio, employing more than 6,000 people across 40+ countries.

Why Medpace? :

When you join Medpace, you become part of an innovative team that brings cutting-edge therapies to market while building a meaningful and rewarding career focused on scientific excellence and improving patient outcomes around the world through continuous learning and cross-functional collaboration.

***Purpose-Driven Work***

* + Work alongside physicians, scientists, and industry-leading experts committed to advancing the global development of medical therapeutics through clinical research excellence

***Collaborative Culture***

* + Contribute to an interactive team environment that empowers decision making, creative thinking, and continuous learning through open communication and mutual trust.
  + Leadership throughout Medpace is both accessible and approachable

***Continuous Growth & Development***

* + Office based environment with on-site mentors
  + Defined career paths with clear advancement opportunities
  + Industry renowned onboarding and training programs designed to accelerate professional development
  + Ongoing training and continuous learning opportunities throughout your career
  + An environment that encourages employees to influence change, contribute ideas, and grow quickly

***Other Employee Benefits***

* + Competitive compensation programs that recognize and reward performance
  + Comprehensive health, wellness, retirement, and PTO benefits
  + Office based culture with occasional WFH that provides flexibility for eligible positions after training
  + Company-sponsored social events

*Please note benefits may vary based on country.*

**What to Expect Next**

A Medpace team member will review your application and if your profile matches our current needs, you will be contacted for an interview. While we review all applications carefully, we are unable to respond to every applicant, and only candidates selected for interviews will be contacted.

*Remote IT Service Desk Analyst (India) – deliver written, English-language IT support to a global manufacturing organisation across Europe, Asia and the United States.*

**This position will be 6 months contract.** (possible to renew when the terms end)

**About the role.** You are the remote first point of contact for IT across our international offices, resolving incidents and service requests through our ticketing platform. Working primarily in writing (with AI-assisted translation), while also handling occasional calls and online meetings, you troubleshoot Microsoft 365, devices and access issues, keep tickets moving to agreed service levels, and coordinate with local IT colleagues when hands-on work is needed on site.

**What you'll do.**

* Handle first- and second-line tickets;
* troubleshoot Windows 11, Microsoft 365, Teams, SharePoint and OneDrive;
* administer accounts, mailboxes, licences and access in Microsoft 365 and Entra ID;
* support users and devices remotely through approved remote-support tools;
* keep clear documentation and knowledge articles;
* and escalate complex issues with full context.

**How we work.**

A fully remote, written-first support model based in India, with a daily overlap with European hours and clear progression towards senior service-desk, team-lead or specialist roles.

You join a global IT team and are employed locally through our Employer of Record arrangement.

Working from home is possible where the candidate’s home-working location has sufficiently fast and stable fibre internet connectivity.

**What we're looking for**

* An IT qualification and at least three years of relevant remote IT support experience;
* demonstrable hands-on knowledge of Microsoft Office, Microsoft 365, Windows 11, Virtual Desktop Infrastructure (VDI), Active Directory, Microsoft Entra ID, printer queues and server-based user administration;
* practical experience using Microsoft Intune for support and troubleshooting;
* structured, service-oriented approach.
* Excellent written and spoken English is a hard requirement.
* Familiarity with ITIL, PowerShell, Intune application packaging, Windows Autopilot, routers and switches, Apple Business Manager and Samsung Knox is an advantage.
